# What Cloudflare must NOT publish.
#
# `wrangler.jsonc` sets `assets.directory` to `.`, so without this file
# the ENTIRE REPOSITORY is uploaded and served. Measured on 2026-09-05
# against the live site: `/handover.md` returned 200 with the real
# position history in it, `/supabase/migrations/0033_*.sql` returned the
# actual purchase records it documents, and `/src/*`, `/supabase/*`,
# `/CLAUDE.md` and `/.env.example` were all readable by anyone. The app
# is password-gated; the files sitting beside it were not.
#
# Gitignore syntax, matched against the assets directory (the repo root).
# A DENY-list rather than an allow-list on purpose: a missed exclusion
# leaves one more file public and is fixable in a minute, while a missed
# ALLOW takes the live site down. Tighten it by adding lines, and verify
# every change by fetching the paths afterwards — the deploy is the only
# thing that can confirm what it actually publishes.
#
# The site is: index.html, assets/, sw.js, workbox-*.js,
# manifest.webmanifest. `_headers` is consumed by the platform rather
# than served, so it stays.

# The record. These quote real holdings and balances.
LEDGER.md
handover.md

# Source, server code and schema. The migrations carry real trade data
# in their comments.
src/
supabase/
scraps/
public/

# Tooling, agent configuration and the ledger package.
.github/
.claude/
.cursor/
.agents/
.ledger/
hooks/
node_modules/

# Repo documentation and configuration.
*.md
package.json
package-lock.json
deno.lock
eslint.config.js
knip.json
.size-limit.json
wrangler.jsonc
.editorconfig
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.nvmrc
.env.example
LICENSE
